  "content": "<div>\n  <p>Over the past several years, we’ve come across some interesting books. Below is just some of the books we recommend:</p>\n</div>\n\n<figure><img src=\"/images/ideas/15484682_image001.jpg\" alt=\"Lung CT scan from the invisible-gorilla study: 83 percent of radiologists missed the gorilla in the top right\" /></figure>\n\n<figure><img src=\"/images/ideas/15484684_51G2EGMP1GL._SX326_BO1_204_203_200_.jpg\" alt=\"SME schedule scrub triad: external experts uncover risks, FMEA the schedule, critical design review for lurking issues\" /></figure>\n\n<figure><img src=\"/images/ideas/15484697_Screen+Shot+2019-01-25+at+6.27.02+PM.png\" alt=\"Reflecting risk in the schedule: identify high-risk tasks, pad durations, add contingency tasks, add learning cycles\" /></figure>\n\n<figure><img src=\"/images/ideas/15484697_Screen+Shot+2019-01-25+at+6.26.09+PM.png\" alt=\"Happy-versus-realistic schedule: optimistic curve slips past target; FTTM pull-in converges before it\" /></figure>\n\n<figure><img src=\"/images/ideas/15484698_image-asset.png\" alt=\"Single-source database bridge: backward-looking metrics and forward-looking indicators off one lateralized source\" /></figure>\n\n<figure><img src=\"/images/ideas/15484699_Screen+Shot+2019-01-25+at+6.31.54+PM.png\" alt=\"Why-do-it and why-not list: see problems early, create urgency, identify decisions today that shape outcomes\" /></figure>\n\n<figure><img src=\"/images/ideas/15484700_image-asset.png\" alt=\"Happy-schedule psychology: wishful thinking and self-fulfilling estimates versus realistic-schedule advantages\" /></figure>\n\n<figure><img src=\"/images/ideas/15484702_image-asset.png\" alt=\"Why teams hide the gap: avoid repercussions, avoid attack, avoid non-team-player label; exposing it forces decisions early\" /></figure>\n\n<figure><img src=\"/images/ideas/15484702_image-asset.png\" alt=\"Why teams hide the gap: avoid repercussions, avoid attack, avoid non-team-player label; exposing it forces decisions early\" /></figure>\n\n<div>\n  <p><br></p>\n</div>",
